# Non-secret, public settings only (ARCHITECTURE §10.3). Never put secrets here.
# Copy to .env for local use; .env is git-ignored. Production values are NOT set
# here and must not be configured without owner approval (§18).

# Canonical origin. MISSING (R11). Leave unset: a reserved .invalid host is used outside
# production. A production build requires exactly https://<apex-domain> (no www, no path,
# no trailing slash) and fails otherwise (src/lib/site-url.ts).
# SITE_URL=

# Build environment (src/lib/env.ts): exactly "production", "preview" or "development",
# or unset. Only "production" enables indexable output; preview/development/unset build
# noindex, nofollow pages (N5). Any other value (e.g. "Production", "prod") is an ERROR in
# both the build and the release check. Netlify CONTEXT=production also means production
# (and then requires a valid SITE_URL); CONTEXT=production with preview/development, or
# CONTEXT=deploy-preview/branch-deploy with production, is a conflict ERROR.
# PUBLIC_SITE_ENV=preview
